info.description:
Build an Arabic library app with public JSON, matching cover images, and original reading samples. This Hono API runs on Cloudflare Workers and supplies the [live Maktabah prototype](https://maktabah-prototype.pages.dev). The catalog contains 12 fictional books in 4 categories, each with 3 sample chapters. Authors, ratings, and full-book page counts are illustrative; full ebook downloads are not available.

No API key or authentication is required. Requests are read-only: use GET, with HEAD and CORS preflight OPTIONS also supported. Successful API responses contain `data` and `meta`; errors contain `error` and `meta`. Arabic text is UTF-8 and should be rendered RTL. Books include an absolute `coverUrl` suitable for Flutter `Image.network`.

Start with `GET /api/v1/home`, list categories with `GET /api/v1/categories`, then explore `GET /api/v1/books`. Search examples below use Arabic text and category IDs. Read `/api/v1/books/light/chapters/0` for a complete sample chapter. Chapter indexes start at 0; display numbers start at 1.

```sh
curl --get 'https://maktabah-demo-api.ashahin.workers.dev/api/v1/books' --data-urlencode 'q=الضوء' --data-urlencode 'category=literature' --data-urlencode 'limit=6'
```

For Flutter, add `http` with `flutter pub add http`. This short example fetches Arabic JSON from the public API; the reusable client in `api/examples/maktabah_api.dart` adds typed catalog pagination, timeouts, and envelope/error checks.

```dart
import 'dart:convert';
import 'package:http/http.dart' as http;

Future<void> main() async {
  final uri = Uri.https(
    'maktabah-demo-api.ashahin.workers.dev',
    '/api/v1/books',
    {'q': 'الضوء', 'category': 'literature', 'limit': '6'},
  );
  final response = await http.get(uri).timeout(const Duration(seconds: 15));
  final body = jsonDecode(utf8.decode(response.bodyBytes)) as Map<String, dynamic>;
  if (response.statusCode != 200) throw Exception(body['error']);
  final books = body['data'] as List<dynamic>;
  print('Found ${books.length} books.');
}
```

Saved books, reading positions, bookmarks, and preferences belong in per-device local storage. Import `/api/v1/demo-state` once when initializing a new store; subsequent fetches must preserve the user's local state. There are no mutation endpoints or server-side user records.

All `/api/v1` endpoints reject unknown or duplicate query keys. Searches with no matches and pages beyond the last page return 200 with an empty array. Unknown resources return 404; invalid queries/indexes return 400; unsupported methods return 405. Trailing slashes are accepted. The [raw OpenAPI contract](https://maktabah-demo-api.ashahin.workers.dev/openapi.json) is available separately from this interactive reference.
